+# Feature Specification: Bulk import
+
+Teams moving from spreadsheets paste many tasks at once; `importTasks(list, text)` adds them.
+
+- **FR-001**: `importTasks` is exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- **FR-002**: The text holds one task per line, as `title;priority;tags`. Lines end with `\n` or `\r\n`.
+- **FR-003**: The priority may be empty (a normal task); the tags are separated by whitespace and may be empty. A line with only a title is valid.
+- **FR-004**: Lines that are empty or only whitespace are skipped.
+- **FR-005**: Every valid line is added to the list through `add`, in order; the result is `{ imported, rejected }`, `imported` being the number of tasks added.
+- **FR-006**: Every line that cannot be added is listed in `rejected` as `{ line, reason }`, `line` counting from 1 over all lines of the text (blank ones included), `reason` saying what is wrong. One bad line does not stop the others.
+- **FR-007**: Rejected: a line with more than three fields, an invalid title, priority or tag (as in `add`), a title already in the list (including one added earlier by the same text).
+- **FR-008**: Never throws (constitution); a rejected line changes nothing in the list.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Fields are trimmed; the priority must otherwise be exactly `low`, `normal` or `high`.
+- A title cannot contain `;`.
